Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element of the split array) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:
- The function to return the second word instead of the first word in multi-word strings
- An IndexError when there was only one word (no index 1 exists)

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now both tests pass successfully.
